================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE / PARITY NOTES
================================================================================
* Data binds through `@Observable TeslaChargingSessionsMapModel` (ADR-004 — no networking in the
  view). The web component takes a `sessions: TeslaChargingSession[]` prop and renders from local
  state; the native model is driven by a `TeslaChargingSessionsMapSource` seam (P1/S8) over the
  charging slice (previews/tests use the in-memory source). Manifest declares NO API data sources.
* The map uses the P3 native MapKit `Map` wrapper only (never a WKWebView). Web Leaflet
  `MapContainer`+`MapTileLayer` -> `Map(position:).mapStyle(.standard(...))`; web `MarkerCluster`
  point -> `Annotation` + brand-accent bolt pin + plotted-count chip; web Leaflet popup / `popupHtml`
  -> a native callout card built from the pure `TeslaChargingSessionCalloutDisplay`.
* Web `center` memo (mean of `lat ?? 0`/`lng ?? 0`, SF `{37.77,-122.42}` default) and `clusterPoints`
  filter (`typeof === 'number' && !Number.isNaN`) are reproduced exactly in `Projection` /`Adapter`,
  covered by unit tests. The camera frames every plotted marker via the shared `TSGeo.boundingRegion`,
  falling back to the `center` memo at a zoom-5-equivalent continental span.
* Units: energy stored SI (Wh) and converted at the display boundary only — web
  `fmtNumber(convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh'),1)` -> `formatEnergyKwh(wattHours:)` (`wh/1000`, 1 dp).
  No non-SI stored/computed (P1/S5, ADR-005).
* Adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): one SwiftUI layer; `.regularMaterial`/`.ultraThinMaterial`
  glass (ADR-005), Dynamic Type, light/dark, VoiceOver labels on the map (`role=application` parity),
  pins, count chip and callout; ≥44pt tap targets.
* Three+ data states for the (single, local) data source: loading -> redacted skeleton; empty ->
  ContentUnavailableView (web EmptyState); error -> retry surface (web QueryError); plus the loaded
  map and a >2-min stale / offline freshness chip (ADR-013). Never a blank region (ADR-011).
* i18n: every visible/spoken string resolves via the P1/S10 facade with the web English fallback
  (ADR-014); the web `tesla_sessions.*` key NAMES are preserved verbatim. The 3 manifest keys also
  pre-exist in the master `Localizable.xcstrings` under the web-bridge `translation.*` namespace.

